@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki To OSB Product Consumption and Purchase Integration
	Testing Koroneiki To OSB Product Consumption and Purchase Integration functionality.

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay OSB Product |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay OSB Product |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORONEKORONE |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create and view product consumption with purchase
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Koroneiki product consumptions with a product purchase created via API should be viewable under Project Details.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Liferay OSB Product | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay OSB Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |                |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |                |
	| Perpetual               | true                     |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1          | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2          | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3          | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |                |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |                |
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Liferay OSB Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Purchase        | true            |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the History tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate the product ID value for "A Liferay OSB Product"
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for "A Liferay OSB Product"
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Purchase" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "quantity" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase        |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | quantity                      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | 1                             |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Purchase" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "accountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase        |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}            |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Purchase" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "productEntryId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase        |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | productEntryId                |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticProductId}            |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Purchase" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "additionalProp1" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase        |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp1               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue1                |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Purchase" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "additionalProp2" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase        |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp2               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue2                |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Purchase" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "additionalProp3" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase        |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp3               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue3                |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Purchase" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "status" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Purchase        |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | status                        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | 0                             |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Consumption" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "productPurchaseId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption     |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | productPurchaseId             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticProductPurchaseId}    |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Consumption" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "accountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption     |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}            |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Consumption" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "productEntryId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption     |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | productEntryId                |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticProductId}            |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Consumption" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "additionalProp1" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption     |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp1               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue1                |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Consumption" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "additionalProp2" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption     |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | additionalProp2               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | propertyValue2                |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Added Product Consumption" and "A Liferay OSB Product" with the field value "additionalProp3" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Added Product Consumption     |
	| Update Description          | A Liferay OSB Product         |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
